    "q-176029": {
      "dom_id": "step-q176029",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "$\\,$ $x∤3$\n\nThe predicate $P(x)$ is given above. Which of following represents $¬P(x)?$",
      "worked_solution": "In plain English, our predicate $P(x)$ means the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x$ does not divide $3.$\n\nThe symbol \"$¬$\" represents negation. So, our task is to negate the given sentence. \n\nTo negate our plain English sentence, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\n$\\,$ It is not true that $x$ does not divide $3$,\n\nIn other words, $x$ divides $3.$ Therefore, $¬P(x)$ means the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x∣3$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
