    "q-176823": {
      "dom_id": "step-q176823",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14253566/assets/41f32abbcc3dec501392378379bceb0d1c111ab4c458d832508f20adb42451e6.png)\n\nThe shaded region above represents the truth set of a predicate $P(x),$ defined over the universal set ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following is the truth set of $¬P(x).$",
      "worked_solution": "The truth set of $¬P(x)$ is the *complement* of the truth set of $P(x):$\n\n$$\n{T}_{¬P}={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\n$$\n\nTherefore, to get the truth set of $¬P(x),$ we take all the points that belong to $U$ and do not lie in ${T}_{p},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14253566/assets/bb2a35ad33731bfe5f26960a518a038b21a9445e38e3647a792326e23fd105ad.png)",
