    "q-175515": {
      "dom_id": "step-q175515",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Find the truth set of $¬P(x)$ given the following predicate defined over the universal set $R:$\n\n$\\,$ $P(x):$ $3x+2>8$",
      "worked_solution": "The truth set of $¬P(x)$ is the *complement* of the truth set of $P(x):$\n\n$$\n{T}_{¬P}={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\n$$\n\nTo find the the truth set of $P(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+2 & >8 \\\\ 3x & >6 \\\\ x & >2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $P(x)$ is\n${T}_{P}=(2,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{¬P} & ={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P} \\\\  & =\\overset{―}{(2,\\infty )} \\\\  & =(-\\infty ,2].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-175515-a",
